From c37874e29c43e86f5ed94d02275f1c31cf68afb3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Neil Horman <nhorman@openssl.org>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 18:02:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Reduce CPU usage for crl_crldp_check

crl_crldp_check rebuilds the full X509_NAME for each crl distribution
point in a certificate.  This operation needs to be preformed for each
crl dp in a cert, time each crl being checked, leading to expoentital
CPU time to execute a verification.  A malicious user can provide a
certificate with a large number of CRL DPs, causing potential DoS on a
system through extended execution time.

Fix it by pre-building the CRLDP full names, before iterating over the
loops, allowing for reuse of those names, rather than having to rebuild
them each iteration

Fixes: openssl/srt#560

Fixes: CVE-2026-121482
Reviewed-by: Mounir Idrassi <mounir.idrassi@idrix.fr>
Reviewed-by: Bob Beck <beck@openssl.org>
Merge-date: Wed Nov 18 20:33:16 2026
Merged-from: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/33546
(cherry picked from commit 54e14955ef7cbea3b82adbc52b52aab8ac76387a)
---
 crypto/x509/x509_vfy.c | 196 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 161 insertions(+), 35 deletions(-)

